.nh
.TH "PB-TUNNEL-DOCTOR" "1" "Sep 2026" "Paperboat" "Paperboat CLI"

.SH NAME
pb-tunnel-doctor - Diagnose tunnel health


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpb tunnel doctor <tunnel> [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Diagnose where a tunnel is failing: placement, the machine's connection, the edge and the
origin. --bundle prints a preview of a bounded support bundle for the absolute path you give,
and writes nothing; add --write-bundle to write exactly the previewed bundle. --bundle-max-bytes
bounds its size (64KiB to 8MiB, default 2MiB).

.PP
JSON output is supported with --json.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB--bundle\fP=""
	absolute path for a local support-bundle preview

.PP
\fB--bundle-max-bytes\fP=2097152
	maximum bundle bytes (64KiB-8MiB)

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for doctor

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	print canonical JSON

.PP
\fB--write-bundle\fP[=false]
	write the exact previewed bundle (requires --bundle)


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--config\fP=""
	path to the CLI config file

.PP
\fB--ephemeral\fP[=false]
	use the temporary preview lifecycle

.PP
\fB--no-customization\fP[=false]
	ignore local shortcuts, command defaults, and TUI preferences

.PP
\fB--server\fP=""
	paperboat-server base URL override

.PP
\fB--workspace\fP=""
	resource workspace selector: personal or a team slug


.SH EXAMPLE
.EX
  pb tunnel doctor web
  pb tunnel doctor web --bundle /tmp/bundle.json
  pb tunnel doctor web --bundle /tmp/bundle.json --write-bundle
.EE


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBpb-tunnel(1)\fP
